{
  "text": " Then they tried to wait her out. The glass was running, and the litter was in the middle, and the tawn's captain stood back and folded her arms, and Kiva understood that the point at the glass would go to whichever half the litter's middle lay in, and the litter's middle was on the line. Prue saw it too. Prue said, very quietly, heads ours, foots theirs, middles on the chalk. Kiva did not move her stance, she could not without shutting, but she leaned, she leaned from the floor, as Anwen leaned, with her knees bent and her weight down, and let the floor push, and the head of the commodore went a hand's breadth west under her forearms, with a scrape of canvas on stone.",
